course: dictionary
lesson: 4628
title: Hill: high ground and a slope
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hill is high ground with sloping sides. It is lower than a mountain. «Ride your bike up the hill» uses the second meaning: a slope on a road or path that you climb or go down.
explain: Context helps you tell the meanings apart. In «The castle stood on a hill», a hill is land you can stand on. In «Ride your bike up the hill», the words bike and up tell you it is a slope to climb.
explain: Hill also appears in phrases. «Over the hill» is a joking way to say someone is past their best because of age. It has nothing to do with land, so check the words around it before you decide what it means.
explain: Maps show hills too. «EU5 shows hills and mountains as terrain pictures», and real maps use contour lines to show how high the land is. When the lines are close together, the hill is steep.
fact: A hill is high ground, lower than a mountain, with sloping sides.
fact: A hill can also be a slope on a road or path, like «ride your bike up the hill».
fact: «Downhill» means going down a slope, and «uphill» means going up one.
fact: «Over the hill» is a joking phrase meaning past your best because of age.
fact: On a map, contour lines join points at the same height, so lines close together show a steep hill.
exercise: «The castle stood on a hill above the valley.» What is a hill? | A river that runs fast | * High ground with sloping sides | A flat field by the sea | A deep hole in the ground
exercise: «Ride your bike up the hill.» In this sentence, what does hill mean? | A grassy plain | A mountain higher than the clouds | * A slope on a road or path | A small lake
exercise: Mia says «over the hill» means she is climbing a big hill. What is the best answer? | It means she is very happy | It means she is climbing a steep slope | * It is a joke that means someone is past their best because of age | It means she has crossed a river
test: On a map, lines close together show what about a hill? | The hill is very quiet | The hill is made of water | The hill has no height at all | * The hill is steep
test: What does «downhill» mean? | Going across a lake | Going up a slope | * Going down a slope | Going round in a circle
exam: In «Taronga Zoo sits on a hill above the harbour», what does hill mean? | A kind of boat | * High ground with sloping sides, where the zoo sits above the water | A type of bird | A slope on a road
